  "interpretation": [
    "Whisper has more substitutions and insertions than the other systems; some short references receive longer text. This describes disagreement with the reference, not verified speech hallucination attribution.",
    "Omni has many deletions and outputs using letter scripts absent from the corresponding references. Unicode scripts are measured mechanically; they are not inferred spoken-language labels.",
    "An output in another writing system may count as one word under the unchanged whitespace-based scorer, so word-count ratios and WER alone do not describe its content; CER is retained alongside them.",
    "A high corpus WER is the aggregate number of word edits divided by reference words, not the percentage of failed requests or an assessment that every word is wrong.",
    "The source excerpts are short and lack surrounding conversational context. This protocol feature is documented, but these outputs do not establish it as the cause of any model ranking."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Four recordings do not represent all Kazakh speakers or conversations.",
    "Original source audio and human references are frozen; no correction, transliteration, model tuning or new inference was performed.",
    "The compared deployable model configurations have different native frontends and language-conditioning capabilities. Results do not isolate architecture, precision or language-conditioning effects."
  ]
